description:
Hello, our name is Customertimes, but you can call us CT. We are a global digital engineering, product development, and technology consulting company. Headquartered in New York, we have a team of 1000+ experts working across 65+ countries.

**About this job:**

* The role is responsible for designing, implementing, and optimizing Salesforce Data Cloud (Data 360) capabilities that support customer data unification, audience creation, and activation across commercial use cases;
* The ideal candidate will serve as a subject matter expert for Salesforce Data Cloud, leading the design of Data Lake Objects (DLOs), Data Model Objects (DMOs), data harmonization, profile matching, and audience frameworks. This role will partner closely with Data Engineering, Business Operations, Commercial Technology, and Marketing teams to ensure scalable and efficient audience management and activation processes;
* The role requires deep expertise in Salesforce Data Cloud architecture, hands-on implementation experience, and the ability to identify opportunities that improve operational efficiency and business adoption.
* Location: India (Remote)
* **How you'll make an impact:**
* Design, develop, and maintain Data Lake Objects (DLOs) and Data Model Objects (DMOs) within Salesforce Data Cloud to onboard and harmonize data from Databricks and other enterprise data platforms;
* Define and implement Data Cloud data models, relationships, and mapping strategies aligned with business requirements;
* Configure and optimize profile matching, unified customer profiles, calculated insights, and data harmonization processes;
* Serve as a technical advisor to operations teams on audience design, segmentation strategies, and Data Cloud best practices;
* Build and manage audience segments to support commercial, marketing, and customer engagement initiatives;
* Design and implement scalable audience activation frameworks leveraging Data Cloud activation capabilities;
* Support data publishing and activation to downstream platforms, including Salesforce Marketing Cloud and other approved third-party solutions;
* Drive operational excellence by identifying opportunities for automation, process optimization, and reusable design patterns;
* Collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders to translate business needs into scalable Salesforce Data Cloud solutions;
* Develop solution documentation, governance standards, and operational procedures to support platform adoption and sustainability.

**What makes you a great fit:**

* Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Engineering, Data Analytics, or
  **a**
  related field;
* 5+ years of experience in customer data platforms, CRM technologies, marketing technologies, or data management;
* 3+ years of hands-on Salesforce Data Cloud (Data 360) experience;
* Proven experience designing and implementing DLOs, DMOs, and Data Cloud data models;
* Experience onboarding and integrating large-scale datasets from Databricks or similar cloud data platforms;
* Strong understanding of profile matching, data harmonization, customer profile unification, and calculated insights;
* Experience building audience segments and supporting audience activation use cases;
* Ability to work independently and engage stakeholders across business and technology organizations;
* Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills.

**Skills:**

* Salesforce Data Cloud (Data 360);
* SFMC Integration;
* Third-party integrations with Data 360;
* Solution Architecture;
* Stakeholder Management;
* Business Consulting

**Skill required:**
Master Data Management - Master Data Management (MDM)


**Designation:**
Sales Prog & Incentive Mgmt Associate


**Qualifications:**
Any Graduation


**Years of Experience:**
1 to 3 years


**About Accenture**
Accenture is a global professional services company with leading capabilities in digital, cloud and security.Combining unmatched experience and specialized skills across more than 40 industries, we offer Strategy and Consulting, Technology and Operations services, and Accenture Song— all powered by the world’s largest network of Advanced Technology and Intelligent Operations centers. Our 784,000 people deliver on the promise of technology and human ingenuity every day, serving clients in more than 120 countries. We embrace the power of change to create value and shared success for our clients, people, shareholders, partners and communities.Visit us at www.accenture.com


**What would you do?**
The Junior Data Management Analyst is responsible for maintaining and securing the accuracy of Master Data in the SAP database, ensuring system integrity and compliance with internal and external procedures. Master Data is a critical information source for SAP systems, supporting most business processes across CLIENT. The role ensures that data is accurate, timely updated, duplicate-free, and managed in a controlled and compliant manner This position also supports users across GBS with Master Data-related issues in systems such as SAP, Blackline, and CRA. The goal is to maintain an error-free, well-governed Master Data environment that ensures smooth operational performance for CLIENT companies.


**What are we looking for?**
University Bachelor’s Degree (Finance, Business, IT, or related field preferred) Additional certifications or SAP training is a plus Bachelor’s degree or diploma holder in a relevant field Basic understanding of SAP systems and database logic Exposure to shared services or multinational working environments is a plus Experience in Master Data creation and maintenance is a plus Strong MS Office skills (Excel, Word, Access, PowerPoint) Good English communication and comprehension skills Analytical thinking, problem-solving, and attention to detail Time management and task prioritization Ability to work under pressure and manage deadlines Effective communication and stakeholder engagement skills


**Roles and Responsibilities:**

* Creation and maintenance of Data objects in accordance with standard procedures of GBS;
* Ensure service levels and targets are consistent with quality and timeliness, and that service is delivered in accordance with agreed TAT.
* Ensuring timeless, accuracy and completeness of all Master Data, identifying and resolving data quality issues;
* Ensure that Data Management processes are in accordance with the internal and external audit requirements;
* Maintaining robust data management policies, procedures and processes, and a robust control environment;
* Ensure a controlled environment in which all reports are accurately and timely rolled out, in line with all global standards;
* Proactively communicate and collaborate with stakeholders to analyse information needs and functional requirements;
* Raise issues to technical team, provide required information, and make active follow-up on open incidents;
* Ensure ad-hoc reports extracted from the system are processed in line with Service Level Agreement (SLA);
* Assist with Monthly / Bi-Annually Cleanse exercises for data objects in scope;
* Deliver trainings to new joiners;
* Ensuring accurate and timely update of TLDs delegated by Data Management (Task Level Descriptions) and the knowledge transfer within the DM team.
